# Rukka Folio — local config. Copy to .env (git-ignored), then `chmod 600 .env`. Never commit .env.
# .env is plain text on disk: it holds identifiers and LOCAL-ONLY throwaway values, never a real secret.
#
# ── 1. Identifiers (not secrets) — docs/ops/lead-times.md §1
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=           # 20-char project ref, region ap-south-1 (Mumbai)
SUPABASE_URL=                   # https://<ref>.supabase.co
#
# ── 2. Local-only values for `supabase functions serve --env-file ../.env` (server/README.md §1)
# Generate fresh on this machine (`openssl rand -base64 32`). Never reuse one on a hosted project,
# and never copy a hosted value down here.
RF_API_DB_URL=                  # postgresql://rf_local:rf_local@<db host>:54329/postgres — seed.sql's local role, [db.pooler]
RF_MAINT_DB_URL=                # postgresql://rf_local_maint:rf_local_maint@<db host>:54329/postgres
RF_JWT_HMAC_KEY=
RF_PHONE_HMAC_KEY=
RF_PHONE_KEK=
RF_ENTITLEMENT_KEY=             # 32-byte Ed25519 seed, base64 (ADR 2026-09-05g §1)
OTP_PROVIDER=fake               # local: sends nothing; msg91 only on pilot/production (server/README.md §5)
PAYMENT_GATEWAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=local-only
#
# ── 3. NOT here — real secrets live in a password manager / macOS Keychain, or only on Supabase
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD     Postgres owner login; bypasses all RLS. Keychain, then type it at the
#                          `supabase link` / `db push` prompt, or pass it for one command:
#                          security add-generic-password -s rukka-folio-dev-db -a postgres -w
#                          SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD="$(security find-generic-password -s rukka-folio-dev-db -w)" supabase db push
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN    run `supabase login` instead of keeping a personal access token in a file.
# Hosted function secrets  RF_API_DB_URL, RF_MAINT_DB_URL, RF_JWT_HMAC_KEY, RF_PHONE_HMAC_KEY, RF_PHONE_KEK,
#                          RF_ENTITLEMENT_KEY, OTP_PROVIDER (+ OTP_PROVIDER_API_KEY, OTP_DLT_ENTITY_ID,
#                          OTP_DLT_TEMPLATE_ID), PAYMENT_GATEWAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, and on the dev project only
#                          RF_DEV_PROJECT_REF — set with `supabase secrets set` (server/README.md §4–§5).
# PAYMENT_GATEWAY_KEY_ID / _KEY_SECRET   gateway console + password manager; no code reads them yet (M13).
# Not needed at all       SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (nothing in app/lib sends it), SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#                          (the functions never read it — lead-times.md §1 step 5, _shared/env.ts).
